# /graphify-to-wiki — Sync Knowledge Graph → Wiki

When the user types `/graphify-to-wiki`, run the integration pipeline that reads graphify output and creates/updates wiki pages using Obsidian-flavored markdown.

---

## Prerequisites

Before running, verify:
1. `graphify-out/graph.json` exists (run `/graphify .` first if missing)
2. `graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md` exists
3. `wiki/index.md` exists (LLM Wiki project initialized)
4. `schema.md` exists (page type definitions)

---

## Pipeline Steps

### Step 1 — Parse Graph Data

Read `graphify-out/graph.json` and extract:

| Data | Source in graph.json | Maps to Wiki |
|------|---------------------|--------------|
| God nodes (highest degree) | `nodes[].edges` count from `links[]` | `wiki/entities/` or `wiki/concepts/` |
| Communities (clusters) | `graph.hyperedges[]` + GRAPH_REPORT communities | `wiki/synthesis/` |
| Surprising connections | GRAPH_REPORT "Surprising Connections" | `wiki/synthesis/` or update `related:` fields |
| Hyperedges (group relations) | `graph.hyperedges[]` | `wiki/comparisons/` |
| Knowledge gaps | GRAPH_REPORT "Knowledge Gaps" | `wiki/queries/` (open questions) |

### Step 2 — Deduplicate Against Existing Wiki

Before creating any page:
1. Read `wiki/index.md` to get all existing page slugs
2. For each candidate node/entity from graphify:
   - Normalize name to kebab-case
   - Check if `wiki/entities/<slug>.md` or `wiki/concepts/<slug>.md` already exists
   - If exists → **UPDATE** (add new connections to `related:` frontmatter, append new info)
   - If not exists → **CREATE** new page

### Step 3 — Generate Wiki Pages (Obsidian Format)

Use `.claude/skills/obsidian-skills/skills/obsidian-markdown/SKILL.md` formatting rules:

#### Entity Page Template
```markdown
---
type: entity
title: "<Node Label>"
tags: [<extracted from graph community>, <node type>]
related: ["[[related-entity-1]]", "[[related-entity-2]]"]
created: <today YYYY-MM-DD>
updated: <today YYYY-MM-DD>
graphify_node_id: "<node id from graph.json>"
confidence: "<EXTRACTED | INFERRED | AMBIGUOUS>"
source_file: "<source_file from graph.json>"
---

# <Node Label>

> [!info] Auto-generated from graphify knowledge graph
> Confidence: <EXTRACTED/INFERRED> | Community: <community number> | Edges: <edge count>

<Description derived from node label and connected edges>

## Connections

<List of [[wikilinks]] to connected nodes, grouped by relationship type>

## Source Context

<Quote or reference from the source_file where this entity was extracted>

## Related Pages
<List of [[wikilinks]] from related: frontmatter>
```

#### Concept Page Template
```markdown
---
type: concept
title: "<Concept Label>"
tags: [<community tags>]
related: ["[[entity-1]]", "[[entity-2]]"]
created: <today YYYY-MM-DD>
updated: <today YYYY-MM-DD>
graphify_node_id: "<node id>"
---

# <Concept Label>

> [!abstract] Knowledge Graph Concept
> Part of Community <N> (Cohesion: <score>) | <edge count> connections

<Description synthesized from node context and edges>

## Key Relationships

<Wikilinked list of edges with relationship types>

## Related Pages
<[[wikilinks]]>
```

#### Synthesis Page Template (from Surprising Connections)
```markdown
---
type: synthesis
title: "Synthesis: <Connection Description>"
tags: [graphify-insight, cross-community]
related: ["[[node-a]]", "[[node-b]]"]
created: <today YYYY-MM-DD>
updated: <today YYYY-MM-DD>
---

# <Connection Description>

> [!tip] Surprising Connection
> This relationship was flagged by graphify's community detection as crossing cluster boundaries.

## The Connection

**[[Node A]]** ←→ **[[Node B]]**

- Relationship: <edge label>
- Confidence: <EXTRACTED/INFERRED>
- Source: `<source_file>`

## Why This Matters

<Brief analysis of why this cross-community link is noteworthy>

## Explore Further
- [[node-a]]
- [[node-b]]
```

### Step 4 — Update Index and Log

After creating/updating pages:

1. **Update `wiki/index.md`** — Add new entries under appropriate type sections
2. **Update `wiki/log.md`** — Append entry:
   ```markdown
   ## <YYYY-MM-DD>

   - [graphify-to-wiki] Synced <N> new pages, updated <M> existing pages from graphify knowledge graph
   - New entities: [[entity-1]], [[entity-2]]
   - New concepts: [[concept-1]]
   - New synthesis: [[synthesis-1]]
   ```

### Step 5 — Post-Sync Validation

After all pages are created:
1. Verify all `[[wikilinks]]` in new pages point to existing files
2. Report any dangling links (targets that don't exist yet)
3. Suggest follow-up actions for knowledge gaps

---

## Usage Patterns

| User says | Action |
|-----------|--------|
| `/graphify-to-wiki` | Full sync: parse graph → create/update all pages |
| `/graphify-to-wiki --entities-only` | Only sync god nodes as entity pages |
| `/graphify-to-wiki --insights-only` | Only sync surprising connections as synthesis pages |
| `/graphify-to-wiki --gaps` | Only create query pages from knowledge gaps |
| `/graphify-to-wiki --dry-run` | Preview what would be created/updated without writing |
| `/graphify-to-wiki --update` | Only update existing pages with new graph connections |

---

## Decision Logic — Entity vs Concept

| Signal | Maps to |
|--------|---------|
| Node is a named tool/repo/person/org | `wiki/entities/` |
| Node is an abstract idea/method/pattern | `wiki/concepts/` |
| Node describes a comparison/tradeoff | `wiki/comparisons/` |
| Node is an open question or gap | `wiki/queries/` |
| Node connects multiple communities | `wiki/synthesis/` |

---

## Obsidian Skills Integration

This rule uses the following obsidian-skills formatting:

1. **Wikilinks** (`[[page-slug]]`) — All cross-references use Obsidian wikilink syntax
2. **Callouts** (`> [!type]`) — Used for metadata boxes (info, tip, warning, abstract)
3. **Frontmatter** (YAML `---` blocks) — Full property support per schema.md
4. **Tags** — In frontmatter `tags: []` array, kebab-case
5. **Embeds** (`![[page]]`) — For embedding related content inline where useful

Reference: `.claude/skills/obsidian-skills/skills/obsidian-markdown/SKILL.md`

---

## Graphify Output Reference

| File | Contains | Used For |
|------|----------|----------|
| `graphify-out/graph.json` | Full graph (nodes, links, hyperedges, metadata) | Entity/concept extraction |
| `graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md` | God nodes, surprising connections, communities, gaps | Prioritization and synthesis |
| `graphify-out/graph.html` | Interactive visualization | Not used in sync (reference only) |

### graph.json Structure

```json
{
  "directed": false,
  "multigraph": false,
  "graph": {
    "hyperedges": [{
      "id": "string",
      "label": "human-readable description",
      "nodes": ["node_id_1", "node_id_2"],
      "relation": "participate_in | form",
      "confidence": "EXTRACTED | INFERRED",
      "confidence_score": 0.0-1.0,
      "source_file": "wiki/path/to/source.md"
    }]
  },
  "nodes": [{
    "id": "unique_node_id",
    "label": "Human-Readable Node Name",
    "file_type": "code | rationale | document",
    "source_file": "path/to/source",
    "source_location": "L123 | null",
    "source_url": "url | null",
    "author": "string | null",
    "community": 0,
    "norm_label": "lowercase label"
  }],
  "links": [{
    "source": "node_id",
    "target": "node_id",
    "relation": "relationship_type",
    "confidence": "EXTRACTED | INFERRED",
    "confidence_score": 0.0-1.0,
    "source_file": "path"
  }]
}
```

---

## Filtering Rules

**Node file_type in graph.json:**
- `"code"` — Skip (pure code functions like main(), slugify())
- `"rationale"` — Skip (docstring descriptions of code)
- `"document"` — **INCLUDE** (meaningful entities, concepts, tools extracted from wiki/docs)

Skip nodes that are:
- `file_type: "code"` or `file_type: "rationale"` — code docs, not wiki content
- Duplicate of existing wiki page content (check `source_file` against existing wiki pages)
- Low-confidence AMBIGUOUS nodes (unless `--include-ambiguous` flag)
- Nodes with only 1 edge (isolated) — unless explicitly requested via `--gaps`

Focus on nodes that:
- Have `file_type: "document"`
- Have ≥3 edges (well-connected)
- Are in communities with cohesion ≥0.15
- Have EXTRACTED or high-confidence INFERRED status
- Represent concepts, tools, methodologies, or named entities

---

## Complete Workflow

```
/graphify .                    ← Build/update the knowledge graph
    ↓
/graphify-to-wiki              ← Sync graph insights → wiki pages
    ↓
Review new pages in wiki/      ← Human verifies auto-generated content
    ↓
/graphify . --update           ← Re-index wiki with new pages (feedback loop)
```

This creates a virtuous cycle: graphify maps → wiki enriches → graphify re-maps with richer context.

---

## Error Handling

| Problem | Resolution |
|---------|-----------|
| `graphify-out/` missing | Prompt: "Run `/graphify .` first to build the knowledge graph" |
| `graph.json` malformed | Report parse error with line number |
| Duplicate slug conflict | Append `-2`, `-3` suffix or merge into existing page |
| Dangling wikilink | Add to "Knowledge Gaps" section in wiki/log.md |
| Too many nodes (>50 new pages) | Batch: create top-10 by edge count first, prompt user to continue |
